  "interpretation": [
    "Both files are static ELF executables built with Go 1.27.0 and run in a scratch filesystem without shared GStreamer or codec libraries. H.264 and AV1 each sustain a median 30 decoded fps at 1280x720, near the configured 5 Mbit/s, for approximately 21 seconds.",
    "All four cases observe zero additional packet loss, decoded drops or freeze duration. Each creates and deletes exactly one WHEP session, then exits normally within 153\u2013177ms after SIGTERM; browser logs are empty.",
    "AMD64 is emulated on the test host. This checks packaged functionality and short source cadence/rate, not native AMD64 performance, impaired-network robustness, physical capture, latency or a device CPU budget.",
    "This repeat includes the current shared WHEP cleanup, source key-frame changes and the v1.30-compatible tunnel handshake backport. Direct local media uses no tunnel or TURN, so it does not independently qualify external transport connectivity."
  ],
